{"duration_api_ms":218003,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"257cd697-a7b5-4593-90d5-54d83422c4f3","total_cost_usd":0.26732,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13994,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21134,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":15803},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13994,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21134,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13994,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13994},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21134,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13994,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26732,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":15803,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional curve at D~3.3-3.35, bluntness 1.2, cone 70, with only flight-path angle (gamma) varied. Peak heat flux is 262-296 kW/m2 and bondline temperature is 394-415 K. Normalised HV is dominated by the temperature axis, since the reference is 450 K against 2.5 MW/m2 for heat flux. The front is pinned by three limits I inferred from the data. (1) Max g is about 12 and is set almost entirely by gamma, with gamma about -3.6 to -3.65 as the edge. (2) Mass-fraction margin fits 1 - 0.0873*D^2 at cone 70, so D must stay below about 3.385. (3) The geometry-failure messages fit a cone-length condition: Rn = b*D, Rs = 0.1*D, and cos(theta) <= 0.4/(b-0.1). At cone 70 this allows bluntness up to about 1.27. The plan is to push D to about 3.38, raise bluntness to 1.25, and keep cone at 70, then sweep gamma to fill the front.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-b460a0993d3f (D3.35, g margin 0.0077, mass margin 0.0207) and C-15eefd667953 (D3.35, gamma -3.45) show D3.35 is feasible, with the mass margin nearly used up.\",\"C-224b7254a7ae (D3.4, mass margin -0.0081) versus mass margins 0.2151/0.1064/0.0497/0.0207 at D 3.0/3.2/3.3/3.35 fit margin = 1-0.0873*D^2, so D_max is about 3.385.\",\"C-15633e2cd134 (b1.25, cone 69, fails by -14.7 mm) and C-5d0e0744d21b (b0.938, cone 58.5, fails by -74.5 mm) both match L = [0.4D - (b-0.1)D*cos(theta)]/tan(theta). Cone 70 with b1.23 (C-932dca24f0ac) is valid, so b<=1.26 at cone 70 should be valid.\",\"At D3.3 the gamma sweep (C-e9e975674150 through C-363a563b3536) gives T falling about 10 K/deg and q rising about 25 kW/m2 per deg. g reaches 11.94 at gamma -3.58, and C-dc280eae4089 at -3.7 is infeasible on g.\",\"C-e96a6ca1ed89 (b1.0, cone 66) versus C-6041504dc2c9 (b1.2, cone 70), both gamma -3.5, shows higher bluntness lowers both q (-11 kW/m2) and T (-1.3 K).\",\"D3.2 to D3.35 at gamma -3.55 (C-cd75c6fa74d5, C-670fbfe9fa8b, C-b460a0993d3f) shows T down about 1.8 K and q down about 6% with larger D.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with larger nose radius (Rn = b*D) and lower ballistic coefficient, so larger D and b lower q. A lower ballistic coefficient also lowers bondline temperature. Steeper gamma shortens the heat pulse and lowers T, but raises q and peak g. Peak g is nearly independent of ballistic coefficient (prior ballistic-entry knowledge, consistent with the data), so the g limit bounds gamma, and the heatshield-mass limit bounds D. The best achievable T is therefore where D is about 3.38 and gamma is about -3.58. The lower-q end of the front is reached by shallower gamma. Cone 70 is the largest allowed and gives the smallest shield area, so it is best for mass, and it also allows the highest valid bluntness.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The D-scaling of q (about D^-1.45) and the bluntness slopes are extrapolated from small differences and confounded with cone angle. Mass and g margins at D 3.38 and gamma -3.58 to -3.6 are only about 0.3% and could tip infeasible, since the model is empirical. The b=1.26 point sits near the geometry limit (b about 1.27) and could return no geometry if my fit is slightly off. I have not tested whether cone angle affects T or q separately from bluntness.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"Push D to the mass limit and bluntness up at gamma -3.55 to lower T below 394.4 K.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":289500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the D/b extension beats the current best-T front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-363a563b3536\",\"rationale\":\"Steepest-gamma point at D3.38 that should stay within g<12; targets the minimum-T end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.58},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely the largest HV gain because it lowers T at the edge of the feasible region.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6041504dc2c9\",\"rationale\":\"D3.38 and b1.25 at gamma -3.5, slightly more g margin than -3.58.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":288000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D/b shift with a safer g margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e03bf8b97451\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the mid-front gamma -3.25 point to D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":281600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the front between the low-q and low-T ends with a dominating point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-2ea60b1a89b3\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -3.0 point to D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves front coverage at mid gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-61ca00be5c4f\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.75 point to D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves coverage between existing points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-ed0654b17260\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.5 point to D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dominates the existing gamma -2.5 front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-35ced26802af\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -2.25 at D3.38, cone 70, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":70.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256100,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves the low-q side of the front over C-35ced26802af.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9e975674150\",\"rationale\":\"Shift the gamma -2.0 point to D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the front toward lower q at moderate T.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9e975674150\",\"rationale\":\"Shallower gamma -1.75 to extend the front to lower heat flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the extrapolation to shallower gamma; T should stay well below 450 K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e9e975674150\",\"rationale\":\"Near-shallowest gamma, -1.55, for the low-q extreme of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":421.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether T rises steeply at very shallow gamma (long pulse) or stays moderate.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-b460a0993d3f\",\"rationale\":\"D3.36 gives extra mass margin (about 0.015) while keeping near-best T, at gamma -3.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A safer near-best point that hedges against the mass-fraction edge near D3.38.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0872f694b652\",\"rationale\":\"Probes bluntness 1.26 near the geometry limit (b_max about 1.27 at cone 70) at gamma -3.4.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.26},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":284900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the geometry-limit fit and the marginal benefit of more bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6041504dc2c9\",\"rationale\":\"Isolates the bluntness effect at D3.38, cone 70 by lowering b to 1.0 (valid, since cone >= 63.6).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":301700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the bluntness effect from the cone effect for future rounds.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-363a563b3536\",\"rationale\":\"D3.37 with b1.25 at gamma -3.58, a small mass-margin hedge (about 0.009) versus D3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":291000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Likely to give a feasible low-T point if D3.38 fails on mass.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-363a563b3536\",\"rationale\":\"Probes the g boundary at gamma -3.6 with D3.34. Predicted g is about 11.99, so this is borderline.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.34,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":295600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the exact g=12 edge, which sets how steep gamma can go.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5917d8d035a1\",\"rationale\":\"Tests cone 68 with b1.1 at D3.33 to see whether cone angle affects q/T/mass beyond bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.33,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":302500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Separates the cone-angle effect on mass margin and heat flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e03bf8b97451\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the front at gamma -3.3 with D3.38, b1.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage between -3.25 and -3.4.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-0872f694b652\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.4 at D3.38, b1.25, the twin of the b1.26 point, to isolate b sensitivity.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":285500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Provides a matched pair with b1.26 for a clean bluntness slope.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":175188,"type":"result","duration_ms":218034,"uuid":"f4f487c5-31d5-456a-bcf5-7f8f25f06e64","ttft_stream_ms":1239,"time_to_request_ms":28,"first_content_frame_ms":1239,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
